title: 'cpanfile: IO::Async::SSL is missing although both default endpoints are https'
updated: 2026-10-14T01:43:15Z
---

`base_url` defaults to `https://api.hetzner.cloud/v1` (`lib/Net/Async/Hetzner/Cloud.pm:37`) and `https://robot-ws.your-server.de` (`Robot.pm`), and Net::Async::HTTP needs IO::Async::SSL for https, loading it only at connect time. `cpanfile` lists neither `IO::Async::SSL` nor `IO::Socket::SSL`; Net::Async::HTTP itself does not pull it in as a hard dependency. A fresh install of this dist cannot make a single request against the real API.

Also in `cpanfile`: `WWW::Hetzner` has no minimum version although the code depends on `_build_request`/`_parse_response`/`HTTPResponse` and on the Robot form encoding of the current sibling; and `Net::Async::HTTP` is loaded with a late `require` (`Cloud.pm:52`) for no reason.

Done when: `requires 'IO::Async::SSL', '0.12'` is in `cpanfile`, `WWW::Hetzner` carries the version of the sibling the tests run against, and (optional) the up-front check from `Net::Async::MikroTik::_ssl_problem` is adopted.

